examples":[{"text":"The disaster was shattering to Mystic’s thousands of alumnae, even if they hadn’t set foot there for decades. […] Within the first hours and days, there were text chains, prayer services, old photos shared on private Facebook pages, and teary alumnae gatherings, including one at the George W. Bush Presidential Center in Dallas. […] Nearly every alumna has a personal story about the family.","ref":"2026 February 24, Ruth Graham, “How the Flood Fractured the Tightknit Camp Mystic Community”, in The New York Times, →ISSN, archived from the original on 24 Feb 2026:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[53,59],[53,60],[243,249],[243,250],[347,353]],"id":"31a47bff-4816-4a45-b89c-3156adf63f9c"}],"links":[["pupil","pupil"],["student","student"],["university","university"],["college","college"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["A female pupil or student (especially of a university or college)."],"id":"1ef3459c-ad6e-483e-acbd-5254bd24f393"},{"links":[["graduate","graduate"]],"glosses":["A female graduate."],"id":"e8ee0472-6cd8-40e7-b330-b4f41c836306"}],"related":[{"word":"alum"},{"word":"alumnae"},{"word":"alumni"},{"word":"alumnus"}],"synonyms":[]},"alum":{"id":"45afbeb0-73ee-4a50-b884-c33bea6cc9b6","word":"alum","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"chemistry: double sulfate","tags":["masculine"],"word":"alume"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"chemistry: double sulfate","tags":["masculine"],"word":"alúmen"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Venice also needed alum for trade, since it was the point of departure for overland transportation of alum to southern Germany and its cloth-manufacturing Free Cities.","ref":"1991, Felix Gilbert, The Pope, His Banker, and Venice, page 80:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[19,23],[102,106]],"id":"b7736dce-fe00-4284-9580-40f475d3abaa"},{"text":"A natural astringent and antiseptic, potassium alum was coveted for its medicinal and cosmetic properties.","ref":"2011, Thomas Penn, Winter King, Penguin, published 2012, page 201:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[47,51]],"id":"d82568de-faf2-440a-b217-feba9d38142f"}],"attestations":[{"date":"from 14th c.","references":[]}],"links":[["astringent","astringent"],["salt","salt"],["crystal","crystal"],["dyeing","dyeing"],["tanning","tanning"],["medicine","medicine"],["sulphate","sulphate"],["potassium","potassium"],["aluminium","aluminium"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"glosses":["An astringent salt, usually occurring in the form of pale crystals, much used in the dyeing and tanning trade and in certain medicines, and now understood to be a double sulphate of potassium and aluminium (K₂SO₄·Al₂(SO₄)₃·24H₂O)."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"8f607950-30ca-4b4d-85e7-d01f10a54471"},{"examples":[{"text":"With weld and cochineal, which are colouring matters the most sensible to the action of sulphate of iron, the purified alums gave us colours more brilliant, fresh, and in a slight degree lighter; while those with our common alums were all duller, and evidently of a deeper hue.","ref":"1807, William Nicholson, editor, A Journal of Natural Philosophy, Chemistry, and the Arts, volume XVIII, page 286:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[119,124],[224,229]],"id":"442138f2-8f6a-4b18-b072-5b8413b1b824"},{"text":"For similar reasons, aluminium sulphate and alums are used in dyeing cloth.[…]Normally alums are soluble in water and insoluble in alcohols.","ref":"2000 June, Competition Science Vision, page 486:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[44,49],[87,92]],"id":"83be814b-0010-465e-8b6c-388362432ee4"},{"text":"In structure, the alums consist of simple ions, being not complexes, but double salts. Potash alum or potassium alum is the common alum, with the formula KAl(SO₄)₂·12H₂O) which, for convenience, may be written K₂SO₄·Al₂(SO₄)₃·24H₂O","ref":"2005, Amit Arora, Text Book Of Inorganic Chemistry, page 386:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[18,22],[18,23],[94,98],[112,116],[131,135]],"id":"110336af-ad5e-429e-9163-2a5fb5c33ad9"}],"topics":["chemistry","inorganic-chemistry","natural-sciences","physical-sciences"],"attestations":[{"date":"from 17th c.","references":[]}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","en:Inorganic compounds"],"links":[["inorganic chemistry","inorganic chemistry"],["potassium","potassium"],["aluminium","aluminium"],["univalent","univalent"],["tervalent","tervalent"],["cation","cation"]],"raw_glosses":["(inorganic chemistry) Any similar double sulphate in which either or both of the potassium and aluminium is wholly or partly replaced by other univalent or tervalent cations."],"glosses":["Any similar double sulphate in which either or both of the potassium and aluminium is wholly or partly replaced by other univalent or tervalent cations."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"7ad47fe8-6629-4f51-a067-57b2e54be78d"}],"related":[{"word":"aluminiferous"},{"word":"aluniferous"},{"word":"aluminiform"},{"word":"aluminilite"},{"word":"aluminise"},{"word":"aluminize"},{"word":"aluminite"},{"word":"aluminous"},{"word":"alunite"},{"word":"alunogen"},{"word":"apjohnite"},{"word":"bosjemanite"},{"word":"halotrichite"},{"word":"kalinite"},{"word":"websterite"}],"synonyms":[{"sense":"double sulphate of potassium and aluminum","word":"potash alum"}]},"aluminosilicate":{"id":"bc2ecb5b-2159-4eb3-abea-f2d64ded5400","word":"aluminosilicate","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"any silicate mineral in which some Si4+ ions are replaced by Al3+","tags":["masculine"],"word":"aluminossilicato"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"topics":["chemistry","inorganic-chemistry","natural-sciences","physical-sciences"],"categories":["English 7-syllable words","English countable nouns","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English nouns","English te